# CEG: bible-project — Hebrew database + translation website
# Repo: kitcosby/bible-project (public; originally cosbykit-afk/bible-project)
# Grounded in website/app_v2.py routes and schema_v2.sql (v2 normalized corpus).
# Public-domain sources only.
#
# v2 normalization (2026-09-28, commits 937ccc7 + 8e71728):
# - schema_v2.sql: base tables normalized (words, verses, root_entry/form/vowel,
#   morph_patterns/segments, strongs_sources, lexicon_* child tables, glosses,
#   kjv_words, ylt_verses/renderings). bible_v2.db opened READ-ONLY by app_v2.
# - Derived-data stage (built after migrate; never alters base tables):
#   build_alignment.py -> word_alignment (836,290 rows; Hebrew/KJV/YLT links);
#   build_variants.py -> word_variants (528,565 rows; v1-medial vs academic-final);
#   apply_morph_corrections.py -> morph_variants (28 rows, 12 words; established
#   corrections re-point words.morph_pattern_id, probable/secondary staged only).
# - app_v2.py: faithful port of app.py to the v2 corpus. Routes, forms, redirects,
#   export format, choice-file format unchanged. Queries read normalized tables;
#   child-table row order preserves v1 blob order so drop-downs render identically.
# - Word detail (v2) additionally shows: Strong's source (strongs_sources),
#   YLT verse contexts (lexicon_ylt_context, resolved refs), Found verses
#   (lexicon_found_verse, resolved refs). Affixes row still from *_disp (U-7).
# - v2 also fixes the /bible "Books" link bug (mount-prefix aware via SCRIPT_NAME).
# - Derived tables (word_alignment, morph_variants) are NOT yet surfaced in the
#   website UI; they are build-pipeline outputs, not modeled here.
# - word_variants IS now surfaced: /variants route (2026-09-30) — Hebrew word
#   drop-down + search box, variant readings table per word (528,565 rows,
#   all variant_kind='spelling' so far; witness/variant_type columns ready).
# - Interlinear view (2026-09-30, Kit-approved wireframe): /interlinear/<b>/<c>/<v>
#   — Hebrew words in Hebrew order (RTL) each with variant + translation
#   drop-downs; English sentence below in KJV word order from word_alignment /
#   kjv_words, KJV words with no Hebrew alignment italicized (KJV print
#   convention); dynamic Book/Chapter/Verse drop-downs via /api/*; Prev/Next
#   verse links roll over chapter and book boundaries; word detail page gains
#   a Bibliomancy section listing every verse using the word form.
# - QA driver (drivers/bible.py) ported to app_v2.py + bible_v2.db 2026-09-28.
# - 2026-09-30 Kit adjudication on export formats: an unrecognized format is
#   NOT invalid (Kit: possibly highly archaic vowel structures) — the app
#   must never reject it. New expectation e18: the export flags the format
#   for further research and still renders the full translation with special
#   characters displayed. Old f5 ("rejects unsupported format") was a model
#   error, not a product bug.
# - Clean reading view (2026-09-30, Kit): /reading/<tid>/<b>/<c>/<v> is now
#   NOTHING but the English translation as exported — no interlinear, no
#   drop-downs, no Hebrew spans, no navigation chrome. Unknown verses 404.
# - User accounts (2026-09-30, Kit): user_accounts table (salted password
#   hashes, never cleartext); /signup, /login, /logout; translations created
#   while logged in record owner_id. Kit's translation-source integer is
#   recorded on lemma_default: 1=KJV, 2=Young's, 3=user-defined (source 3
#   links to other_option via other_option_id).
# - Variant de-dup (2026-09-30, Kit): the v1-medial vs academic-final rows
#   are NOT real manuscript variance — dirty data from the study tool, which
#   ignored special characters for end-of-word letterforms. Rows differing
#   ONLY by medial/final letterforms (fold_finals) are folded away and never
#   baked into the UI. Kit 2026-10-01: v1 data-artifact rows (basis marking
#   anomaly= or ARTIFACT) are excluded from variant display entirely — only
#   academic/textual manuscript variants count. No textual rows are loaded
#   yet, so the /variants drop-down is empty with an explanatory note until
#   real apparatus data arrives. Words with no real variance show "none"
#   instead of the drop-down (interlinear).
# - DB QA applications (2026-11-11, Kit-approved; issues #20/#21/#23):
#   verse-grid repair refiled 92 misfiled words to their true verses
#   (Esth 4:4, Ps 17:1, Isa 27:1, Jer 28:1, Lam 2:1 filled); 18 exact
#   Strong's fills applied (blank Strong's now 4,321 in both stores);
#   split_multi_strongs resolved as COMPOSITE values in words.strongs
#   (comma-joined in maqqef-chain order, components in strongs_components,
#   source oshb-split; 135 words) — new cause c19 / effect e41;
#   PARALLEL-CONFLATE distribution pass on ylt_renderings (357,574 rows;
#   shared YLT positions 11,448 -> 10,642); local corpus and production
#   PostgreSQL verified in full content-hash parity (words, YLT,
#   word_alignment, lexicon_ylt_rendering).
# - Hidden verse shells (2026-11-11, Kit ruled "leave the rows but hide
#   them"): the 7 verse rows emptied by the grid repair (Ps 17:17,
#   Isa 27:22, Jer 28:23, Lam 2:23, Josh 4:32, 2 Chr 36:32, Ruth 8:18)
#   are KEPT in the grid (each retains its Peshitta no_counterpart note)
#   and flagged verses.hidden = 1 in schema_v2.sql and both stores.
#   app_v2 honors the flag in the shared _WORDS_EXIST fragment, the HTML
#   book/chapter listings, and the read-view navigation helpers
#   (_chapter_bounds, _last_chapter) — new cause c18 / effects e40, f11.
#   Verified live in production 2026-11-11: /api/chapters/8 = [1,2,3,4],
#   /api/verse/19/17/17 = 404, /api/verses/19/17 = 1..15, read view for
#   Ruth 4 offers no chapter-8 navigation.

[PAGE]
Bible website pages (v2): index, book, chapter, verse, choice (POST),
translations, reading, export, word detail, variants, interlinear, signup,
login. Database: bible_v2.db (v2 normalized).

[INPUTS]
c0 = page : index | book | chapter | verse | choice | translations | reading | export | word | variants | interlinear | signup | login
c1 = ref_valid : no | yes
c2 = translation_id : none | kjv | ylt | custom
c3 = choice_submit : no | yes
c4 = export_format : none | supported | unsupported
c5 = word_id : invalid | valid
c6 = affixes_present : no | yes
c7 = strongs_source_present : no | yes
c8 = ylt_contexts_present : no | yes
c9 = found_verses_present : no | yes
c10 = variant_search : empty | text
c11 = variant_word : none | valid | invalid
c12 = variants_present : no | yes
c13 = nav_dynamic : no | yes
c14 = verse_edge : first | middle | last
c15 = bibliomancy : none | listed
c16 = auth : logged_out | logged_in
c17 = credentials : right | wrong
c18 = verse_hidden : no | yes
c19 = strongs_form : single | composite

[CONSTRAINTS]
# (page is always selected; no constraint needed — every combination is a real page state)

[SUCCESS]
e1 = index lists the books
e1 <= c0=index
e2 = book page lists its chapters
e2 <= c0=book AND c1=yes
e3 = chapter page lists its verses
e3 <= c0=chapter AND c1=yes
e4 = verse page shows the text in KJV
e4 <= c0=verse AND c1=yes AND c2=kjv
e5 = verse page shows the text in YLT
e5 <= c0=verse AND c1=yes AND c2=ylt
e6 = verse page shows the text in the custom translation
e6 <= c0=verse AND c1=yes AND c2=custom
e7 = choice POST sets the translation and redirects back
e7 <= c0=choice AND c3=yes AND c2=kjv
e8 = choice POST sets the translation and redirects back
e8 <= c0=choice AND c3=yes AND c2=ylt
e9 = choice POST sets the translation and redirects back
e9 <= c0=choice AND c3=yes AND c2=custom
e10 = translations page lists and manages translations
e10 <= c0=translations
e11 = reading view renders the passage in the chosen translation
e11 <= c0=reading AND c1=yes AND c2=kjv
e12 = reading view renders the passage in the chosen translation
e12 <= c0=reading AND c1=yes AND c2=ylt
e13 = export produces the file in the requested format
e13 <= c0=export AND c4=supported
e14 = word detail shows the Affixes row from the normalized disp columns
e14 <= c0=word AND c5=valid AND c6=yes
e15 = word detail shows the Strong's source from the normalized strongs_sources table (v2)
e15 <= c0=word AND c5=valid AND c7=yes
e16 = word detail shows YLT verse contexts from lexicon_ylt_context with resolved references (v2)
e16 <= c0=word AND c5=valid AND c8=yes
e17 = word detail shows found verses from lexicon_found_verse with resolved references (v2)
e17 <= c0=word AND c5=valid AND c9=yes
e18 = export with an unrecognized format flags it for research and still renders the translation with special characters displayed
e18 <= c0=export AND c4=unsupported
e19 = variants page shows the Hebrew word drop-down (empty with an explanatory
      note until academic/textual variants are loaded; v1 data-artifact rows
      excluded per Kit 2026-10-01)
e19 <= c0=variants
e20 = search filters the drop-down to matching Hebrew words
e20 <= c0=variants AND c10=text
e21 = selecting a valid word with variants shows its variant readings table
e21 <= c0=variants AND c11=valid AND c12=yes
e22 = index page links to the variants page
e22 <= c0=index
e23 = interlinear page renders the verse's Hebrew words in Hebrew order, each with a translation drop-down and, where the word has real variants, a variant drop-down
e23 <= c0=interlinear AND c1=yes
e24 = interlinear nav offers Book/Chapter/Verse drop-downs; the chapter list follows the book and the verse list follows the chapter (via /api/*)
e24 <= c0=interlinear AND c1=yes AND c13=yes
e25a = at the first verse of a chapter, the Prev link rolls back to the last verse of the previous chapter (or previous book)
e25a <= c0=interlinear AND c1=yes AND c14=first
e25b = at the last verse of a chapter, the Next link rolls forward to the first verse of the next chapter (or next book)
e25b <= c0=interlinear AND c1=yes AND c14=last
e26 = word detail lists every verse using the word, each linking to its verse page (bibliomancy)
e26 <= c0=word AND c5=valid AND c15=listed
e27 = interlinear page renders the English sentence in English (KJV) word order with supplied words italicized
e27 <= c0=interlinear AND c1=yes
e28 = saving a non-default choice records the rendering as the lemma default (Strong's-keyed) for subsequent occurrences of the same word
e28 <= c0=choice AND c3=yes AND c2=kjv
e29 = a later occurrence of the same word shows the propagated choice selected with no explicit per-word save
e29 <= c0=verse AND c1=yes AND c2=kjv
e30 = reading view shows only the English translation text: no Hebrew spans, no drop-downs, no navigation chrome
e30 <= c0=reading AND c1=yes AND c2=kjv
e31 = signup creates the account and logs the user in
e31 <= c0=signup
e32 = login with correct credentials authenticates the user
e32 <= c0=login AND c17=right
e33 = translations created while logged in are owned by that user
e33 <= c0=translations AND c16=logged_in
e34a = saving a KJV choice records translation source 1 (KJV) on the lemma default
e34a <= c0=choice AND c3=yes AND c2=kjv
e34b = saving a Young's choice records translation source 2 (Young's) on the lemma default
e34b <= c0=choice AND c3=yes AND c2=ylt
e34c = saving a user-defined choice records translation source 3 (user-defined) on the lemma default, linked to other_option
e34c <= c0=choice AND c3=yes AND c2=custom
e35 = words with no real variants show "none" instead of a variant drop-down; words with real variants keep the drop-down
e35 <= c0=interlinear AND c1=yes
e36 = every standard page (index, book, chapter, verse, word, variants, translations, interlinear, signup, login) references the papyrus tile background
e36 <= c0=index
e37 = the variants drop-down lists only words having two or more distinct variant readings after medial/final letterform folding
e37 <= c0=variants
e38 = a word's KJV drop-down options are the lemma's distinct full KJV phrases, one option per phrase with this verse's phrase first, never split into separate words
e38 <= c0=verse AND c1=yes AND c2=kjv
e39 = a word's Young's drop-down options are the lemma's distinct full Young's phrases, one option per phrase with this verse's phrase first, never split into separate words
e39 <= c0=verse AND c1=yes AND c2=ylt
e40 = listings and read navigation omit hidden verses: chapter lists contain no chapter whose verses are all hidden (Ruth offers chapters 1-4 only), verse lists exclude hidden verses, and Prev/Next navigation never lands on a hidden verse
e40 <= c18=yes
e41 = a composite Strong's entry (comma-joined maqqef chain, e.g. H853,H3605,H834) resolves on its own word page by exact match as a single lemma; its components do not individually claim the word
e41 <= c0=word AND c5=valid AND c19=composite

[FAIL]
f1 = book page shows not-found for an invalid reference
f1 <= c0=book AND c1=no
f2 = chapter page shows not-found for an invalid reference
f2 <= c0=chapter AND c1=no
f3 = verse page shows not-found for an invalid reference
f3 <= c0=verse AND c1=no
f4 = reading view shows not-found for an invalid reference
f4 <= c0=reading AND c1=no
f6 = word detail 404s on an invalid word id
f6 <= c0=word AND c5=invalid
f7 = variants page shows "Unknown word id" for a nonexistent word id
f7 <= c0=variants AND c11=invalid
f8 = variants page shows "No variants recorded" for a word with no variants
f8 <= c0=variants AND c11=valid AND c12=no
f9 = interlinear page shows not-found for an invalid reference
f9 <= c0=interlinear AND c1=no
f10 = login with wrong credentials is rejected
f10 <= c0=login AND c17=wrong
f11 = a hidden verse shows not-found on verse, interlinear, and reading pages, and /api/verse returns 404 {"error": "not found"} for it, exactly as for an invalid reference
f11 <= c18=yes

[REQUIREMENTS]
REQ-BB-001 : index lists the books -> e1
REQ-BB-002 : book and chapter pages list chapters and verses for valid references -> e2, e3
REQ-BB-003 : verse page renders the text in KJV, YLT, and the custom translation -> e4, e5, e6
REQ-BB-004 : the choice POST switches translation and redirects back -> e7, e8, e9
REQ-BB-005 : translations page lists and manages translations -> e10
REQ-BB-006 : reading view renders a passage in the chosen translation, showing only the English text -> e11, e12, e30
REQ-BB-007 : export produces the requested format; unrecognized formats are flagged for research and never rejected -> e13, e18
REQ-BB-008 : invalid references show not-found on book, chapter, verse, and reading pages -> f1, f2, f3, f4
REQ-BB-009 : word detail shows the Affixes row from the normalized disp columns; invalid ids 404 -> e14, f6
REQ-BB-010 : v2 word detail shows Strong's source, YLT verse contexts, and found verses from normalized child tables -> e15, e16, e17
REQ-BB-011 : variants page offers the Hebrew word drop-down (only words with two or more distinct variant readings) with search, shows variant readings for a selected word, and handles unknown/empty cases; index links to it -> e19, e20, e21, e22, e37, f7, f8
REQ-BB-012 : interlinear page shows each Hebrew word with translation and (where real) variant drop-downs, dynamic Book/Chapter/Verse navigation, Prev/Next rollover across chapter and book boundaries, the English sentence in English word order with supplied words italicized, words with no real variance show "none", and invalid references show not-found; word detail lists every verse using the word (bibliomancy) -> e23, e24, e25a, e25b, e26, e27, e35, f9
REQ-BB-013 : a non-default choice becomes the new lemma default (Strong's-keyed, forward-only) for the rest of the text: the choice POST records it and later occurrences of the same word render it -> e28, e29
REQ-BB-014 : user accounts: signup creates the account and logs the user in; login authenticates with correct credentials and rejects wrong ones; translations created while logged in are owned by that user -> e31, e32, f10, e33
REQ-BB-015 : the choice POST records Kit's translation-source integer on the lemma default: 1=KJV, 2=Young's, 3=user-defined (linked to other_option) -> e34a, e34b, e34c
REQ-BB-016 : site-wide papyrus visual theme: every standard page references the papyrus tile background -> e36
REQ-BB-017 : translation drop-downs offer each source's full per-occurrence phrases as single choices, one option per phrase, never split across lines -> e38, e39
REQ-BB-018 : verses flagged hidden (verses.hidden = 1; the 7 emptied grid-repair shells, Kit 2026-11-11) are retained in the data but never render: not-found on verse/interlinear/reading and via the API, and absent from chapter/verse listings and read navigation -> e40, f11
REQ-BB-019 : composite Strong's values (maqqef chains) are first-class lemmas: stored comma-joined in words.strongs with components in strongs_components (source oshb-split), and their word pages resolve by exact match -> e41
